  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "The probability of drawing a red ball from box A is \\(2/3\\), and from box B it is \\(1/3\\). The 2 boxes are equally likely to be chosen. Given that a red ball was drawn, what is the probability that it came from box A?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "2/3",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Given a red draw, the required probability is A's share of all red draws. Equal box selection gives an A-and-red probability of \\((1/2)(2/3)=1/3\\); the total red probability adds the disjoint contributions from both boxes, \\(1/3+(1/2)(1/3)=1/2>0\\). Therefore the conditional probability is\n\\[\n\\frac{1/3}{1/2}=\\frac23.\n\\]",
